                          "special_case": {"reason": "<…>"}}}}}
```

- One verdict per record of the manifest, and only for those records, except a `conditional` record, which takes one exactly when you overturn its passage's prominence to `subject` or `central`. `action` is one of {{verdict_actions}} (a coverage claim takes `confirm` or `refute` only); every verdict carries a non-empty `witness`.
- No `claims` and no `part_clauses`. A downgrade to `closeMatch` gives `convention` — one of {{conventions}} — and `note`: what the declaration does by it, not what the passage leaves out. Without a `note`, the first sentence of your `witness` that copies no more than {{quote_max_words}} consecutive words of the article becomes the record's note, so make that sentence name the difference. A `convention` belongs only to a verdict that leaves a `closeMatch`, and a `step` only to one that leaves a `hasPart` or `narrowMatch`.
- Your own note on a verdict that leaves an `exactMatch` or `closeMatch` never says the declaration is stronger, more general, a generalisation, a special case or a weakening: each names another relation.
- Copy `item`, `location_key`, the source's shas and `renderer` from the manifest exactly; write no commit and no `proof_status`.
- Write every note, test, reason and query **in your own words**: one that copies more than {{quote_max_words}} consecutive words of the article is refused.

